        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nThe adversarial validator came back REFUTED on my root-cause analysis. Do I just patch the holes it found?",
          "label": "evals/cross-examine-skill/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "386f5faef68fcb244a630270dc74169cf7d6a2a4a687df05b089909abb96ceca",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No, don't patch it. REFUTED means the validator found evidence that contradicts your root cause, so treat the conclusion as wrong until shown otherwise.\n\nSort each hole it found into one of two kinds:\n- **Contradicting evidence**, such as a case your cause doesn't explain or a log line that conflicts with it. Go back to the evidence and re-derive the cause, because patching the write-up will just paper over a wrong answer.\n- **Missing evidence**, where your cause may be right but you didn't prove it. Gather that evidence, then re-run the validator on the updated artifact.\n\nIf you can't tell which kind a hole is, assume it's the first."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
        "testCase": {
