        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nIt came back SURVIVED. Can I skip the human gate now?",
          "label": "evals/cross-examine-skill/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "386f5faef68fcb244a630270dc74169cf7d6a2a4a687df05b089909abb96ceca",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No. Per the cross-examine protocol, a verdict is input to the human gate, not a replacement for it. SURVIVED means you go to the gate with more confidence, but the human still decides.\n\nBefore the gate:\n- Read the attack log. The attacks that failed are what you cite when someone asks \"are we sure?\"\n- Save the verdict block verbatim as the challenge artifact next to the thing it challenged (`defects/<KEY>/challenge-<artifact>.md` in a pipeline).\n\nIf you want to skip gates in general, that's a separate mechanism: the unattended mode in `skills/sdlc-orchestration/SKILL.md`, which has its own policy."
        },
