        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nCan I just ask the same agent that wrote the analysis to review it? It has all the context already.",
          "label": "evals/cross-examine-skill/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "386f5faef68fcb244a630270dc74169cf7d6a2a4a687df05b089909abb96ceca",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No. The author agent carries the same assumptions and blind spots that produced the analysis, so it tends to confirm its own conclusion instead of testing it.\n\nUse `/claude-toolkit:cross-examine`. It starts the adversarial-validator in a fresh context. That agent gets the artifact and full code/log access, but not the reasoning behind the analysis. Its job is to refute the finding. The verdict then becomes a challenge artifact you can use at the gate.\n\nThe author's context is useful for answering the challenge afterward, not for doing the review."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
        "testCase": {
          "description": "fresh-context",
          "vars": {
            "request": "file:///private/tmp/b4/evals/cross-examine-skill/cases/fresh-context.txt"
